  Local diagnostic patch: cache the original first-smallbin predicate's
  address-valid result and observed F->bk, then call an optional failure
  hook only when the existing corruption branch is taken. No additional
  dereference, allocator policy change or disabled safety check is added.
  This file is no longer byte-identical to upstream. The host runner
  reverses only this documented patch and checks the original SHA256.

mspace.c
  Derived from platform/src/dlmalloc/mspace.c at the same SDK commit.
  Original SHA256: fe483dc1f5b3ee6691432724e96a0ac733517a485d947cb6cc0e82b4b62169a5
  Copyright (C) 2026 Mihawk; GPL-3.0-or-later.
  Local changes: USE_LOCKS=2 with allocator_lock.h, and terminal
  CORRUPTION_ERROR_ACTION/USAGE_ERROR_ACTION diagnostics through the title.
  The first-smallbin failure hook records arena, bin, P, F, index, observed
  backlink, original request and the failed predicate in a fixed BSS ring.
  It never reads a chunk header merely to include it in the log. The index
  gives expected chunk size; actual damaged header size is not observed.
  FOOTERS=1, MMAP_CLEARS=0, 32-byte alignment, 16 MiB granularity,
  32 MiB mmap threshold and 64 KiB mapping units remain unchanged.

allocator_lock.h
  Local GPL-3.0-or-later implementation of the dlmalloc custom-lock contract.
  Four-byte atomic ownership matches Sonic SDK pin
  95c08f27386fc698f6bbe21dde3030140a41d10b and its released binary.
  The implementation deliberately differs from Sonic after contention:
  after 64 failed attempts it requests a 50 us nanosleep, preserving errno.
  This addresses the starvation concern documented by SDK commit
  3752be7e7812713e01fbe998d92952cd7b559f7f while retaining atomic ownership.
  No pthread mutex, allocator or emulated-TLS calls occur in this lock.
  Native errno is read/restored only around the slow-path nanosleep.

Integration
  Only this complete mspace translation unit replaces SDK mspace.o.
  SDK heap.c still supplies eight arenas and direct-memory mappings;
  ../heap_wrap_prospero.c replaces the complete SDK heap_wrap.o provider.
  Its marked implementation body differs from SDK heap_wrap.c only in
  function names/linkage, with the same ownership routing and native fallback.
  Public noinline wrappers add bounded entry/exit events with original API
  caller addresses, arguments and return values; nested wrapper calls remain
  visible. The host runner restores names/linkage and requires byte identity.
  All mstate layout readers/writers live together in malloc.c.
  The title defines noreturn prospero_heap_failure(kind, operation, line,
  mspace, pointer). Macro __LINE__ identifies the invocation site and
  may be shared by multiple checks in a nested macro; __func__ names
  the enclosing allocator operation. Detection remains terminal.

Scope
  This is a targeted compatibility change, not proof that lock choice
  caused the previously observed heap corruption or that PS5 execution passes.
